help.guide = Welcome to Vorleser!\n\nThis guide is in the text field so you can have it read to you right away: just press F5. Press F7 to stop.\n\nReading text from other programs\nSelect the text, for example in your browser, in Word or in a PDF, and press {read}. Press the keys again to stop. {pause} pauses and resumes. {mouse} on the selected text opens the Vorleser menu.\n\nRecognizing text on the screen\nFor text you cannot select, such as in images or scanned documents: press {ocr} and drag a frame around the text with the mouse. Vorleser recognizes it and reads it aloud.\n\nOpening files\nUse File, Open, or drop a file onto this window to open Word files, PDFs, e-books, text files and images.\n\nIn the window\nF5 reads from the cursor, F6 pauses, F7 stops. Alt with the left or right arrow jumps back or forward one sentence. Ctrl and S saves the text as an MP3 file.\n\nVoices\nChoose voice and speed in the "Voice" menu or under Tools, Settings, and listen to them with "Sample". "AI voices" downloads particularly natural-sounding voices that then work without internet. The bottom of the window shows the current voice.\n\nVorleser keeps running when you close this window. The speaker icon at the bottom right next to the clock opens it again. Settings are under Tools, and this guide is always available under Help.
